122.9 9. Reference Implementation
The accompanying libraries ship a small, tested Kernel PCA estimator in all three languages, built directly from the equations above: the Gram matrix, the centered kernel \(\tilde K = HKH\), the eigenproblem \(\tilde K\boldsymbol{\alpha} = \mu\boldsymbol{\alpha}\), the normalization \((\boldsymbol{\alpha}^k)^\top\boldsymbol{\alpha}^k = 1/\mu_k\), and out-of-sample projection that reuses the stored training row and grand means. The three implementations are validated against a single shared fixture set, so the numbers below agree across languages to within \(10^{-9}\).
The example below fits an RBF Kernel PCA on six points in the plane and projects both the training set and a new out-of-sample point \(\mathbf{z} = (0.5, 0.5)\) onto the leading kernel principal components.

